  'P0170': ['Fuel trim malfunction (bank 1)\nPossible causes: Fuel System- Excessive fuel pressure. Leaking fuel injector(s). Leaking fuel pressure requlator. Low fuel pressure. Plugged injector(s). Damaged/disconnected HO2S (1.3L O2S) circuit. Induction System- Air leaks after the MC-VAF/MAF. Vacuum leaks. Restricted air inlet. PCV system. Base Engine- Oil overfill. Cam timing. Compression. Ignition- Coil and secondary side of ignition system', 'Fuel Trim Bank 1'],
  'P0171': ['System Too Lean Bank 1\nPossible causes: FUEL SYSTEM; Low fuel pressure; Leaking fuel pressure regulator; Contaminated injector(s) INDUCTION SYSTEM; Air leaks after the MAF sensor; Vacuum leaks; PCV system; Fuel vapor purge system; Air flow obstruction to MAF heated wire; Improperly seated dipstick; Damaged MAF sensor IGNITION; Spark plugs; Plug wires; Coils EGR; Leaking gasket; Leaking diaphragm BASE ENGINE; Cam timing; Cylinder compression; Exhaust leaks before or near the HO2S\'s Note: The PCM monitors the HO2S sensors for measuring O2 in the exhaust system. A misfire will cause a lean condition due to the unburned oxygen in the combustion chamber', 'Bank 1 Long Term Fuel Trim, Range 1 Lean Lower Limit Exceeded', 'Bank 1 long term fuel trim, range 2 leanness lower limit exceeded'],
  'P0172': ['System Too Rich Bank 1\nPossible causes: FUEL SYSTEM; High fuel pressure; Leaking fuel pressure regulator; Contaminated/Leaking injector(s). INDUCTION SYSTEM; Restricted air inlet; PCV system; Fuel purge system; Obstruction to MAF heated wire; Damaged MAF. EGR; Stuck open EGR valve. BASE ENGINE; Oil overfill; Cam timing; Cylinder compression. Note: The PCM monitors the HO2S sensors for measuring O2 in the exhaust system. If all of the oxygen is used for combustion and excess fuel vapor is unburned, a rich condition will exist', 'Bank 1 Long Term Fuel Trim, Range 2 Rich Upper Limit Exceeded', 'HO2S sensor mixture constantly lean'],
  'P0173': ['Fuel trim malfunction (bank 2)\nPossible causes: Fuel System- Excessive fuel pressure. Leaking fuel injector(s). Leaking fuel pressure requlator. Low fuel pressure. Plugged injector(s). Damaged/disconnected HO2S (1.3 O2S) circuit. Induction System- Air leaks after the MC-VAF/MAF. Vacuum leaks. Restricted air inlet. PCV system. Base Engine- Oil overfill. Cam timing. Compression. Ignition- Coil and secondary side of ignition system', 'HO2S sensor mixture constantly rich', 'Fuel Trim Bank 2'],
  'P0174': ['System Too Lean Bank 2\nPossible causes: FUEL SYSTEM; Low fuel pressure; Leaking fuel pressure regulator; Contaminated injector(s). INDUCTION SYSTEM; Air leaks after the MAF; Vacuum leaks; PCV system; Fuel vapor purge system; Air flow obstruction to MAF heated wire; Improperly seated dip stick; Damaged MAF IGNITION; Spark plugs; Plug wires; Coils. EGR; Leaking gasket; Leaking diaphragm. BASE ENGINE; Cam timing; Cylinder compression; Exhaust leaks before or near the HO2S\'s Note: The PCM monitors the HO2S sensors for measuring O2 in the exhaust system. A misfire will cause a lean condition due to the unburned oxygen in the combustion chamber'],
  'P0175': ['System Too Rich Bank 2\nPossible causes: FUEL SYSTEM; High fuel pressure; Leaking fuel pressure regulator; Contaminated injector(s). INDUCTION SYSTEM; Restricted air inlet; PCV system; Fuel purge system; Damaged MAF EGR; Stuck open EGR valve. BASE ENGINE; Oil overfill; Cam timing; Cylinder compression. Note: The PCM monitors the HO2S sensors for measuring O2 in the exhaust system. If all of the oxygen is used for combustion and excess fuel vapor is unburned, a rich condition will exist'],
