  'P0400': ['EGR system flow malfunction', 'EGR Valve Stuck', 'EGR \'A\' Flow'],
  'P0401': ['EGR "A" Flow Insufficient Detected', 'EGR system insufficient flow detected', 'EGR Insufficient Flow Detected', 'Intake Air Temperature sensor (IAT) circuit malfunction\nPossible causes: Open in IAT circuit; Damaged IAT sensor; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0110'],
  'P0402': ['EGR System Excessive Flow Detected', 'EGR "A" Flow Excessive Detected', 'MAF Sensor Circuit Low Input', 'EGR system excessive flow detected at idle', 'EGR Excessive Flow Detected', 'Fuel Temperature Sensor circuit malfunction\nPossible causes: Short to ground or open; Damaged Fuel Temperature sensor; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0180', 'EGR Control Circuit'],
  'P0403': ['EGR Control Circuit', 'EGR valve position control circuit', 'EGR Valve Control Circuit Short', 'Throttle Position(TP) sensor out of self test range\nPossible causes: Loose TP sensor at throttle body; Binding or sticking throttle linkage; Mis-adjusted throttle stop; Damaged TP sensor; Damaged PCM. Note: Diagnostic Trouble Code(DTC) is set when Power Train Control Module detects TP sensor circuit above closed throttle voltage, but below maximum voltage. Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0120', 'Exhaust Gas Recirculation "A" Control Circuit/Open', 'EGR \'A\' Control Circuit / Open'],
  'P0404': ['EGR Control Circuit Failure', 'EGR "A" Control Circuit Range/Performance', 'EGR valve position control performance or range fault', 'EGR Valve Motor Temperature Problem', 'EGR circuit range/performance malfunction\nPossible causes: Damaged EGRC solenoid; Improper harness connection; Improper or damaged hoses; Open/Short in harness (VPWR,EGRC); Damaged PCM. Note: DTC P0404 indicates a malfunction in the EGR control (EGRC) solenoid or EGR vent solenoid circuit'],
  'P0405': ['EGR Sensor A Circuit Low', 'EGR valve position control circuit', 'EGR Valve Position Sensor Circuit Low Input to PCM', 'Crankshaft Position Sensor (Gear)\nPossible causes: Open or short in CKP sensor circuit. Open or short in sig rtn. Open wiring harness shield. Damaged CKP sensor. Damaged flywheel. Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P1336'],
  'P0406': ['EGR Sensor A Circuit High', 'EGR valve position control circuit', 'EGR Valve Position Sensor Circuit High Input to PCM'],
  'P0407': ['EGR Sensor B Circuit Low'],
  'P0408': ['EGR Sensor B Circuit High', 'EGR(B) circuit high'],
  'P0409': ['EGR Valve Position Sensor Circuit Failure', 'EGR valve position sensor', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor Slow Response (HO2S-11)\nPossible causes: Contaminated HO2S-11; Shorted or Open wires; Exhaust leaks; Excessive fueling; MAF meter; Air leaks; Damaged HO2S-11; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0133', 'EGR Sensor \'A\' Circuit'],
  'P040A': ['EGR Temperature Sensor Circuit', 'EGR Temperature Sensor \'A\' Circuit'],
