  'P040C': ['EGR Temperature Sensor Circuit Low', 'EGR Temperature Sensor \'A\' Circuit Low'],
  'P040D': ['EGR Temperature Sensor Circuit High', 'EGR Temperature Sensor \'A\' Circuit High'],
  'P040E': ['EGR Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic', 'EGR Temperature Sensor \'A\' Circuit Intermittent/Erratic'],
  'P040F': ['EGR Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation'],
  'P0410': ['AIR circuit malfunction', 'Secondary Air Injection Valve Circuit Electrical Malfunction', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor Circuit High Voltage (HO2S-11). Rich\nPossible causes: Shorted HO2S-11 signal circuit to Heater Circuit; Shorted HO2S-11 signal circuit to VPWR; Damaged HO2S-11; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0132', 'Secondary Air Injection system malfunction\nPossible causes: Damaged vacuum hoses; Inoperative AIRB / AIRD valve(s); Inoperative Air Pump; Damaged AIRB /AIRD solenoid(s); Open and / or short in AIRB / AIRD solenoid circuit; Damaged PCM', 'AIR System \'A\''],
  'P0411': ['AIR Incorrect Flow Detected', 'Secondary Air Injection System Bank 1 Flow Too Low', 'Heated oxygen sensor circuit out of range low voltage (O2S-11). Lean\nPossible causes: Contaminated HO2S-11 (water,fuel,etc.). Crossed HO2S-11 signal/signal return wiring. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0131', 'ISC was not able to control low idle speed during engine running test', 'AIR System \'A\' Incorrect Flow Detected'],
  'P0412': ['ISC Unable To Control High Idle Speed', 'Secondary Air Injection Valve Circuit Electrical Malfunction', 'Heated oxygen sensor circuit no activity detected (HO2S-11)\nPossible causes: Open or short in HO2S-11 circuit; Improper harness connection; Intake air system; Fuel system; Ignition system; Damaged sensor; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0134', 'AIR System Switching Valve Circuit Malfunction', 'AIR System Switching Valve \'A\' Circuit'],
  'P0413': ['AIR system open circuit', 'AIR System Switching Valve \'A\' Circuit Open'],
