  'P0453': ['EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch \'A\' Circuit High', 'Evaporative emission control system malfunction', 'EVAP canister purge valve circuit fault', 'Evaporative Emission Control system pressure sensor high input\nPossible causes: Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) signal circuit open; FTP signal shorted to VREF or VPWR; VREF shorted to VPWR; Signal Return open; Damaged FTP sensor; Damaged PCM'],
  'P0454': ['EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch \'A\' Circuit Intermittent', 'EVAP sensor intermittent'],
  'P0455': ['Evaporative Emission Control system leak detected (Gross Leak)\nPossible causes: Fuel filler cap missing or damaged; Fuel vapor control valve or fuel vapor valve stuck closed; Loose, cracked or cut fuel vapor hoses in evaporative emissions systems; Pinched or blocked fuel vapor hoses in evaporative emission system; Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) sensor damaged; Damaged CV solenoid; Damaged Vapor Management Valve (VMV); CV circuit open or shorted to VPWR; EVAP canister leaking; Aftermarket parts and accessories nonconforming to the EVAP specifications; Fuel Vapor Vent Valve assembly blocked. Note: Please reference 1998 or later PCED diagnostics for this code', 'EVAP System Leak Detected - Large Leak'],
