  'P050F': ['Brake Assist Vacuum Too Low'],
  'P0510': ['Closed throttle position switch malfunction\nPossible causes: Open or short in harness; Damaged idle switch (in throttle position sensor); Damaged PCM', 'Idle switch fault', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor Circuit High Voltage (HO2S-12). Rich\nPossible causes: Shorted HO2S-12 signal circuit to Heater Circuit; Shorted HO2S-12 signal circuit to VPWR; Damaged HO2S-12; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0138', 'Closed Throttle Position Switch'],
  'P0511': ['PCM internal fault', 'IAC circuit fault', 'IAC valve circuit fault', 'Heated oxygen sensor circuit out of range low voltage (O2S-12). Lean\nPossible causes: Contaminated HO2S-12 (water,fuel,etc.). Crossed HO2S-12 signal/signal return wiring. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0137', 'Idle speed control actuator - open circuit or short to ground/battery voltage', 'Idle Air Control Circuit'],
  'P0512': ['Starter Request Circuit', 'PCM internal fault', 'Engine Switch Circuit High Input to PCM', 'Heated oxygen sensor circuit no activity detected (HO2S-12)\nPossible causes: Open or short in HO2S-12 circuit; Improper harness connection; Intake air system; Fuel system; Ignition system; Damaged sensor; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0140'],
  'P0513': ['The battery voltage level is too low', 'Incorrect Immobilizer Key'],
  'P0514': ['Battery Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance', 'EGR Position Sensor system| - EGR Valve Position (EVP) sensor circuit malfunction\nPossible causes: Damaged EVP sensor; Damaged EGR valve; Open and / or short in EVP sensor circuit; Improper harness connection; Damaged PCM Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P1402', 'EGR System High Flow rate\nPossible causes: Damaged EGR vacuum regulator solenoid valve; Damaged EGR valve, leaking or stuck open; Damaged EGR temperature sensor; Damaged EGR control system modulator valve; Damaged PCM Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P1402'],
