  'P0603': ['KAM internal control module error', 'PCM Fault', 'PCM EEPROM', 'Power interruption on KAPWR circuit', 'PCM KAM error', 'Cylinder 6 Misfire Detected\nPossible causes: Ignition System; Fuel injectors; Fuel Pressure; Evaporative System; Canister Purge; Base Engine; Running out of fuel. Note: Running out of fuel may turn on the MIL and possibly store a Continuous Misfire DTC. Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0306', 'PCM self test - non volatile memory write error', 'Internal Control Module Keep Alive Memory (KAM) Error'],
