  'P0700': ['CAN communication fault', 'Transmission Control System malfunction', 'Transmission Control System (MIL Request)'],
  'P0701': ['Transmission Control System Range/Performance', 'Random/Multiple Cylinder Misfire Detected\nPossible causes: Ignition Systems; Fuel Injectors; Fuel Pressure; Evaporative System; Canister Purge; Base Engine; Running out of fuel. Note: Running out of fuel may turn on the MIL and possibly store a Continuous Misfire DTC. Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0300'],
  'P0702': ['Transmission Control System Electrical', 'Catalyst System Efficiency Below Threshold Bank 1\nPossible causes: Improper vehicle spark timing; Use of leaded fuel; Oil contamination; Damaged HO2S; Damaged ECT sensor; Improperly connected downstream HO2S wires; Fuel pressure too high; Damaged exhaust system pipe; Damaged exhaust manifold; Damaged muffler / tailpipe assembly; Damaged catalytic converter Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0420'],
  'P0703': ['Brake Switch B Input Circuit', 'BOO switch circuit fault', 'Brake Switch \'B\' Circuit'],
  'P0704': ['Clutch switch input circuit malfunction', 'Evaporative emission control system pressure sensor malfunction\nPossible causes: Open between Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) sensor and VREF; Damaged FTP sensor; Restricted carbon canister vent; Damaged Canister Vent (CV) solenoid filter; Kink or blockage in vapor hose/tube between CV solenoid and atmosphere; Short to PWR GND in CV signal circuit; Damaged CV solenoid; Damaged PCM Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0450', 'Clutch switch - implausible signal', 'CLTHSW Input Circuit', 'Clutch Switch Input Circuit', 'DTC P0704:XX-YY is listed as P0704[XX] on workshop materials. Failure part/circuit P0704 = Clutch oil pressure switch failure Failure type (XX above) 12 = Clutch oil pressure switch failure 2 13 = Clutch oil pressure switch failure 1 Current/historical DTC If status byte [YY] is [01] or [09], it is a current DTC. If the status byte is [08], it is a historical DTC. ------- Ignore the information below. It is not necessary for diagnosing this DTC'],
  'P0705': ['TR Sensor circuit in range fault', 'Transmission range sensor electrical circuit malfunction', 'Evaporative Emission (EVAP) control system malfunction (small leak, neg pressure test)\nPossible causes: Damaged vapor line between EVAP Canister Purge valve and intake manifold; Damaged EVAP Canister Purge valve; Damaged vapor line between EVAP Canister Purge valve and vapor storage canister; Damaged vapor line between charcoal canister and storage canister; Damaged vapor line between check valve and fuel vapor valves; Damaged check valve; Damaged fuel vapor storage canister; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0440', 'Transmission Range Sensor Circuit Malfunction. (MLP)', 'Transmission Range Sensor \'A\' Circuit (PRNDL Input)'],
  'P0706': ['Inspect connectors for signs of damage, water ingress, corrosion, etc', 'TR Sensor Circuit Range/Performance', 'PRNDL circuit range/performance proble', 'Transmission Range(TR) Sensor Circuit range/performance\nPossible causes: Mis-adjusted linkage or TR Sensor; Open or Shorted Shift Solenoid(s) circuitry; Damaged TR sensor; Damaged Shift solenoid(s); Damaged internal transmission component(s); Damaged PCM; Intermittents in above', 'Transmission range sensor circuit range/performance', 'Transmission Range Sensor \'A\' Circuit Range/Performance'],
  'P0707': ['TR Sensor Circuit Low Input', 'Transmission Range Switch Circuit Low Voltage', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor(HO2S) Circuit Malfunction Bank 1 Sensor 2\nPossible causes: Short/open HO2S circuit; Exhaust leak; Intake Air system; Fuel system; Ignition system; Damaged HO2S sensor. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0136', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor Slow Response (HO2S-12)\nPossible causes: Contaminated HO2S-12; Shorted or Open wires; Exhaust leaks; Excessive fueling; MAF meter; Air leaks; Damaged HO2S-12; Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0139', 'Transmission Range Sensor \'A\' Circuit Low'],
  'P0708': ['TR sensor circuit High input', 'Transmission Range Switch Circuit High Voltage', 'Steering wheel gearshift control buttons', 'Transmission Range Sensor \'A\' Circuit High'],
