  'P0901': ['Clutch Actuator Circuit Range or Performance', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor(HO2S) Heater Circuit Malfunction Bank 1 Sensor 1\nPossible causes: Shorted/open HO2S circuit; Shorted/open HO2S heater circuit; Damaged HO2S sensor. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0135', 'Clutch \'A\' Actuator Control Circuit Range/Performance'],
  'P0902': ['Clutch Actuator Circuit', 'Clutch Actuator Circuit Low', 'Gear Shift Clutch Solenoid Short to Ground (OFF Fault)', 'Heated Oxygen Sensor(HO2) Heater Circuit Malfunction Bank 1 Sensor 2\nPossible causes: Shorted/open HO2S circuit; Shorted/open HO2S heater circuit; Damaged HO2S sensor. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P0141', 'Clutch \'A\' Actuator Control Circuit Low'],
  'P0903': ['Clutch Actuator Circuit', 'Clutch Actuator Circuit High', 'Gear Shift Clutch Solenoid Short to Battery (ON Fault)', 'Clutch Solenoid Off Failure', 'Evaporative Emission Control system vent control malfunction\nPossible causes: Open between Fuel Tank Pressure (FTP) sensor and VREF; Damaged FTP sensor; Restricted carbon canister vent; Damaged Canister Vent (CV) solenoid filter; Kink or blockage in vapor hose/tube between CV solenoid and atmosphere; Short to PWR GND in CV signal circuit; Damaged CV solenoid; Damaged PCM Note: Equivalent OBDII DTC P0446', 'Clutch \'A\' Actuator Control Circuit High'],
  'P0904': ['Gate select position circuit', 'Select Stroke Sensor Fault / Select 456 Switch Circuit Fault', 'Gate Select Position Circuit \'A\''],
  'P0905': ['Crankshaft Position Sensor (Gear)\nPossible causes: Open or short in CKP sensor circuit. Open or short in sig rtn. Open wiring harness shield. Damaged CKP sensor. Damaged flywheel. Damaged PCM. Note: Equivalent to OBDII DTC P1336', 'Gate select position circuit range/performance', 'Select Switch Short Circuit', 'Gate Select Position Circuit \'A\' Range/Performance'],
